g about v5.19 where each agent needs to add:\n```\n\"tools\": {\n \"allowlist\": [\"message\", \"channels\"]\n}\n```\n\nThis seems like they're asking about a specific change in OpenClaw 5.19 where messaging tools need explicit allowlisting per agent. Let me check the agent-level tools config more carefully.\n\nFrom the config schema output I found earlier:\n- Per-agent tools config has `allowlist` (tool allowlist additions)\n- Per-agent also has `messageActionAllowlist` for message actions like \"send\"\n\nThe user's format `{\"tools\": {\"allowlist\": [\"message\", \"channels\"]}}` doesn't match the per-agent structure I found. \n\nLooking at what they're describing - allowing `message` and `channels` tools - this aligns with the messaging profile which includes `message` and related session tools. But the schema shows `allowlist` and `alsoAllow` are arrays for tool IDs, and there's a separate `messageActionAllowlist` for fine-grained message actions. The format they provided doesn't quite fit either pattern, so I need to reconsider what they're actually asking for.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"callba9cf3a662484d8588c923bebab7c4ef","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"openclaw config schema 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndef find_tools_structure(obj, path=''):\n    if isinstance(obj, dict):\n        if 'tools' in obj.get('properties', {}):\n            print(f'Found tools at {path}')\n            print(json.dumps(obj['properties']['tools'], indent=2)[:4000])\n            print('---')\n        for k,v in obj.items():\n            find_tools_structure(v, path+'.'+k if path else k)\n    elif isinstance(obj, list) and len(obj) > 0:\n        find_tools_structure(obj[0], path)\nfind_tools_structure(d)\n\" 2>/dev/null"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"openclaw config schema 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json,sys\\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\\ndef find_tools_structure(obj, path=''):\\n    i