 engineering, agentic tool use, and office productivity workflows. It is presented as a model deeply participating in its own evolution, with support for complex agent harnesses, dynamic tool search, Agent Teams, and high-fidelity coding and document-editing tasks.\\n\\nThis model is ready for commercial/non-commercial use.\\n\\nThis model is not owned or developed by NVIDIA. This model has been developed and built to a third-party's requirements for this application and use case; see link to Non-NVIDIA [MiniMax M2.7 Model Card](https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M2.7)\\n\\nGOVERNING TERMS: The trial service is governed by the [NVIDIA API Trial Terms of Service](https://assets.ngc.nvidia.com/products/api-catalog/legal/NVIDIA%20API%20Trial%20Terms%20of%20Service.pdf); and use of this model is governed by the [NVIDIA Open Model License](https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/agreements/enterprise-software/nvidia-open-model-license/). Additional Information: [Modified MIT License](https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M2.7/blob/main/LICENSE-MODEL). [MiniMax M2.7](https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M2.7).\\n\\nGlobal\\n\\nUse Case: Designed for advanced coding assistance, agentic workflows, long-horizon software engineering, live production troubleshooting, office document generation and editing, and other complex multi-step productivity tasks.\\n\\nBuild.NVIDIA.com: 04/11/2026 via [link](https://build.nvidia.com/minimaxai/minimax-m2.7)\\n\\nHuggingface: 04/11/2026 via [link](https://huggingface.co/minimaxai/minimax-m2.7)\\n\\nReferences:\\n\\n- [MiniMax M2.7 model page](https://www.minimax.io/models/text/m27)\\n\\n- [MiniMax M2.7 launch report](https://www.minimax.io/news/minimax-m27-en)\\n\\n- [MiniMax M2.7 Hugging Face repository](https://huggingface.co/MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M2.7)\\n\\n- [MiniMax M2.7 GitHub repository](https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/MiniMax-M2.7)\\n\\n- [MiniMax text generation docs](https://platform.minimax.io/docs/guides/text-generation)\\n\\n- [MiniMax model release notes](https://platform.minimax.io/docs/release-notes/models)\\n\\n- [MiniMax API platform](https://platform.minimax.io/docs/guides/models-intro)\\n\\n- [OpenRoom](https://github.com/MiniMax-AI/OpenRoom)\\n\\nArchitec\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"f285d3c8cccdca93\\\">>>\",\n  \"warning\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1e87614ffee1d35a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Fetch\\n---\\nResponse body truncated after 750000 bytes.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1e87614ffee1d35a\\\">>>\"\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779337062645},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[assistant turn failed before producing content]"},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The page didn't show rate limit info. Let me search more specifically for NVIDIA NIM rate limits.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"calla58760559eaf48889dc55afbbeea03d1","name":"web_search","arguments":{"query":"NVIDIA NIM API rate limit requests per minute"},"partialArgs":"{\"query\":\"NVIDIA NIM API rate limit requests per minute\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779337062656,"errorMessage":"429 status code (no body)"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"calla58760559eaf48889dc55afbbeea03d1","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"NVIDIA NIM API rate limit requests per minute\",\n  \"provider\": \"duckduckgo\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1144,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"duckduckgo\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fc8463bc71221200\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAPI Rate Limit Increase for NVIDIA